\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces {\color  {blue}Overview of the experimental pipeline. (1)~Data preparation and $K_0$ baseline establishment across three backbones (Qwen~2.5~1.5B, Gemma~3~1B, Gemma~4~E2B). (2)~Recursive training over ten generations with strict data replacement. (3)~Pressure manipulation along five axes: rank, learning rate, method, module topology, and synthetic-data dose (0/10/25/50\% removal). (4)~Per-generation evaluation of factual retention ($K_0$), effective rank, response length, Distinct-$n$, MTLD, and stopword ratio. (5)~Regime classification (Homeostatic, Bounded, Degradative). (6)~Pressure-regime mapping: effective training pressure identified as the organizing principle for regime transitions.}}}{8}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
